            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>THIS DEMONSTRATION FILING WAS PREPARED BY AUDITCHAIN LABS AG FOR THE STAFF OF THE SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION IN CONNECTION WITH ITS COMMENT ON PROPOSED REGULATION CRYPTO ASSETS (FILE NO. S7-2026-27). IT IS NOT A FILING AND IS NOT AN OFFER OF SECURITIES. DATES ARE ILLUSTRATIVE.</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>THIS OFFERING WILL COMMENCE ONLY UPON FINAL ADOPTION OF REGULATION CRYPTO ASSETS BY THE COMMISSION. THE COMPANY MAY SEEK NO-ACTION RELIEF FROM THE STAFF OF THE COMMISSION TO CONDUCT THE OFFERING UNDER THE PROPOSED RULE AS PUBLISHED. THE LEGAL ENTITY IDENTIFIER SHOWN IS THAT OF AUDITCHAIN LABS AG, USED AS A PLACEHOLDER UNTIL PACIOLI LABS, INC. OBTAINS ITS OWN. THE COMMENT LETTER ASKS THE COMMISSION TO REQUIRE AN LEI OF EVERY ISSUER AND TO OPEN THE FUNDRAISING EXEMPTION TO NON-U.S. ISSUERS. </strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>AUDITCHAIN LABS AG BELIEVES THAT THE LOOK, FEEL AND FUNCTION OF PERFORMING DISCLOSURE OBLIGATIONS UNDER REGULATION CRYPTO ASSETS SHOULD TAKE A FORM AND SHAPE THAT ISSUERS AND USERS OF CRYPTO ASSETS ALREADY KNOW. </strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>THIS SAMPLE IS PREPARED ON BEHALF OF PACIOLI.AI™ FROM THE REGULATION CRYPTO ASSETS DISCLOSURE MODEL SO THAT EVERY STATEMENT IN IT IS MACHINE READABLE AND CAN BE VALIDATED BY THE NETWORK OF STRUCTURED DISCLOSURE VALIDATORS IT DESCRIBES.</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>THE COMPANY IS IN DISCUSSIONS WITH STRUCTURED DATA STANDARD SETTERS ABOUT SERVING AS MASTER CONFORMANCE VALIDATORS. NO AGREEMENT HAS BEEN REACHED WITH ANY OF THEM. THE FEES THAT THE MASTER CONFORMANCE VALIDATORS WILL CHARGE HAVE NOT BEEN SET. THE TWO STANDARD SETTERS THAT THE DOCUMENTS DATED AFTER THE FIRST CLOSING DESCRIBE AS SERVING ARE AN ILLUSTRATION. NO STANDARD SETTER, PROFESSIONAL SERVICES FIRM OR REGULATOR HAS AGREED TO TAKE A SEAT ON THE GOVERNANCE COUNCIL THAT THIS DOCUMENT DESCRIBES.</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>PLACEHOLDERS IN THIS DEMONSTRATION (FICTITIOUS UNLESS STATED): THE INDEPENDENT ACCOUNTANT (THORNBURY & VALE LLP), THE PLACEMENT AGENT (HARROW STREET SECURITIES LLC), THE SECURITY AUDITOR (IRONVAULT SECURITY LABS) AND THE RESULT AND THE PUBLICATION OF ITS AUDIT, THE NODE HOSTING PROVIDER (NORTHSTAR NODE HOSTING LLC) AND ITS LEGAL ENTITY IDENTIFIER, THE THIRD DIRECTOR (AVERY LINDQVIST), THE FOUR KEY HOLDERS OTHER THAN THE COMPANY AND THEIR SEATING AT LAUNCH, THE SMART CONTRACT ADDRESSES (THE PATTERN 0xA0D7... IDENTIFIES THEM AS PLACEHOLDERS), THE TRANSACTION IDENTIFIERS (TXIDS) OF THE SMART CONTRACT DEPLOYMENTS (THE PATTERN 0xD7A0... IDENTIFIES THEM AS PLACEHOLDERS), THE DIGITAL TOKEN IDENTIFIER 7XK9P2D4Q (THE REAL IDENTIFIER IS ASSIGNED BY THE DTI FOUNDATION ON REGISTRATION OF THE TOKEN CONTRACT), THE RIGHTS TO CLAIM THAT THE COMPANY INTENDS TO AWARD TO RELATED PERSONS, THE DATES AND COUNTS OF NODE SALES AND ADMISSIONS, THE PRICES OF ETH ($4,000) AND POL ($0.40) HELD FLAT, THE ADMISSION OF THE COMPANY TO THE POLYGON POS VALIDATOR SET, THE COMBINED INCOME TAX RATE OF 27 PERCENT, THE NETWORK STATISTICS IN THE BLOCKCHAIN NETWORK PARTICIPATION SCHEDULES (TOTAL STAKE, VALIDATOR COUNTS, UPTIME, THE STAKING REWARDS AND THE HOSTING FEE OF $500 PER MONTH), AND THE AFFILIATE'S PARTICIPATION FIGURES, WHICH MIRROR THE COMPANY'S. THE TRADING VENUES NAMED ARE THOSE ON WHICH THE COMPANY INTENDS TO SEEK TRADING OF AUDT AFTER THE FILING OF FORM TR; NO VENUE HAS AGREED TO LIST AUDT. THE EXPENDITURES IN THE FINANCIAL STATEMENTS ARE ILLUSTRATIVE AND ARE NOT IN THE PROPORTIONS OF THE USE-OF-PROCEEDS PLAN OF THE OFFERINGS. NO AUDT HAS BEEN BOUGHT BACK, AND MOST OF THE TREASURY RESERVE IS UNSPENT.</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>FURTHER PLACEHOLDERS: THE AMOUNTS OF AUDT SUBSIDIES PAID EACH MONTH BEFORE THE FILING OF FORM TR (50,000 AUDT A MONTH FROM JULY 2027 THROUGH DECEMBER 2027, 60,000 AUDT A MONTH FROM JANUARY 2028 THROUGH NOVEMBER 2028 AND 40,000 AUDT IN DECEMBER 2028, A TOTAL OF 1,000,000 AUDT, WHICH IS THE CAP); THAT THE SOURCE CODE OF LUCASUITE AND OF THE PACIOLI EXPLORER IS NOT PUBLIC; THAT PACIOLI LABS, INC. SETS AND PUBLISHES ITS PRICES FOR PREPARATION, AND THAT AUDITCHAIN LABS AG OFFERED THE CLOUD SERVICE UNTIL THE LICENSE TOOK EFFECT; THAT THE TREASURY SHARE OF THE PROCEEDS IS A CASH RESERVE THAT THE COMPANY MAY USE FOR ITS OPERATIONS AFTER THE FILING OF FORM TR; THAT THE SHARE OF A TAXONOMY DEVELOPER THAT TAKES NO REWARD IS DIVIDED AMONG THE OTHER RECIPIENTS OF A VALIDATION FEE; THE CEILING OF 4,500,000 AUDT ON CONSULTATION REWARDS; AND THE GROUNDS ON WHICH A VLEI MAY BE REFUSED OR REVOKED. THE LINK TO THE SOURCE CODE WILL BE REPLACED.</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>UNITS OF COVERED INVESTMENT CONTRACT IN THE NODE OFFERINGS ARE PACIOLI VALIDATING NODES - 50,000 AUDT DELIVERED STAKED, WITH THE NODE SOFTWARE LICENSE - AT $50,000 (STARTUP OFFERING) AND $62,500 (TIER 2 NODE OFFERING). RULE 101(E) AS PROPOSED WOULD COUNT ONE AUDT AS ONE UNIT; THOSE EQUIVALENTS ARE REPORTED ALONGSIDE IN THE FUNCTIONAL-UNIT ELEMENTS SO THAT THE COMMISSION CAN READ THE OFFERING EITHER WAY. THE COMMENT LETTER RECOMMENDS THAT AN ISSUER BE PERMITTED TO DEFINE THE UNIT AS A FUNCTIONAL UNIT - THE CRYPTO ASSET TOGETHER WITH THE SOFTWARE OR OTHER TECHNICAL PRIMITIVES IT INVOKES - SO THAT INSTITUTIONS CAN STAND UP A NETWORK THAT INCLUDES THE SOFTWARE THE CRYPTO ASSET OPERATES, AND SO THAT THE EXEMPTION IS EASIER TO USE FOR BUILDING REAL UTILITY THAN FOR A TOKEN SALE WITH NOTHING BEHIND IT.</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>THIS DEMONSTRATION DEPARTS FROM THE PROPOSED RULE IN TWO WAYS THAT THE COMMENT LETTER ASKS THE COMMISSION TO PERMIT. FIRST, RULE 100 AS PROPOSED DEFINES A COVERED INVESTMENT CONTRACT AS AN INVESTMENT CONTRACT TO WHICH NO ASSET OTHER THAN THE CRYPTO ASSET IS SUBJECT, AND REQUEST FOR COMMENT 6 ASKS WHETHER THE DEFINITION SHOULD PERMIT OTHER ASSETS. A UNIT IN THE NODE OFFERINGS INCLUDES THE NODE SOFTWARE LICENSE. SECOND, THE PROPOSED RULE WOULD REQUIRE A MACHINE-READABLE FORMAT ONLY FOR PART I OF FORM 1-CRYPTO AND OF FORM 1-KC, AND THE BODY OF EACH FORM WOULD BE IN HTML. THIS DEMONSTRATION PRESENTS EVERY DISCLOSURE IN MACHINE-READABLE FORM.</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>FORM 1-SU, TO WHICH THIS DOCUMENT REFERS, IS NOT A FORM OF THE PROPOSED RULE. THE PROPOSED RULE WOULD HAVE THE RULE 103 INFORMATION OF A STARTUP-EXEMPTION OFFERING POSTED ON A WEBSITE ONLY (RULE 200(D)); THE COMMENT LETTER RECOMMENDS THE FORM (REQUEST FOR COMMENT 65).</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>THIS TIER 2 OFFERING STATEMENT IS FILED MORE THAN EIGHT MONTHS AFTER THE COMPANY'S FISCAL YEAR-END AND IS QUALIFIED MORE THAN NINE MONTHS AFTER IT, SO IT INCLUDES THE AUDITED STATEMENTS FOR THE PERIOD FROM FORMATION TO DECEMBER 31, 2026 AND UNAUDITED INTERIM STATEMENTS FOR THE SIX MONTHS ENDED JUNE 30, 2027 (FORM 1-CRYPTO PART F/S (B)(3)(II)). THE QUALIFICATION DATE SHOWN IS ILLUSTRATIVE.</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color:hsl(0, 75%, 60%);\"><strong>FURTHER PLACEHOLDERS (OCTOBER 16, 2026): THE ADDRESS AND TXID OF THE KEY HOLDER CONTRACT ON POLYGON POS; THE NUMBER OF ACTIVE PVNS IN EACH MONTH (PVNS THAT VALIDATED OR ANALYZED DISCLOSURES AS THE WINNING PVN OR AS A CORROBORATING PVN IN THAT MONTH) THAT A FILING DOES NOT STATE, USED TO SPLIT THE AUDT SUBSIDIES EQUALLY AMONG ACTIVE PVNS, INCLUDING THE COMPANY'S, WHICH IS ASSUMED TO BE ACTIVE IN EVERY MONTH; THE AMOUNTS OF AUDT AND USDC THAT THE COMPANY INTENDS TO PLACE ON EACH TRADING VENUE. THE PATTERNS 0XA0D7... AND 0XD7A0... IDENTIFY ADDRESSES AND TXIDS AS PLACEHOLDERS.</strong></span></p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 20
        },
