        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT4e0473a06c",
          "@type": "regca:MaximumUnitsToBeOffered",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT4e0473a06c",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 71,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-rst:NumericFactValue",
            "cmns-qtu:hasNumericValue": {
              "@value": "670",
              "@type": "xsd:decimal"
            },
            "cmns-qtu:hasMeasurementUnit": "xbrli:pure",
            "xbrlb:decimals": "INF"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 51
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT9dbf4792bf",
          "@type": "regca:CurrentStageOfDevelopmentDescription",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT9dbf4792bf",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 72,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>Pacioli Labs, Inc. (the \"Company,\" the \"Issuer,\" \"we,\" \"us\" or \"our\") was formed in Delaware on September 30, 2026. On that date, we entered into a license agreement with Auditchain Labs AG (\"Auditchain\"). Auditchain is organized in Switzerland and is an affiliate under common control with us. Jason Meyers, our Chief Executive Officer, controls both Auditchain and us. Under the license agreement, Auditchain granted us a perpetual, global and exclusive license to the Pacioli.ai™ software (the \"Auditchain License\"). The Auditchain License gives us the right to sublicense the software to any third party.</p><p>The Pacioli.ai™ software consists of LucaSuite™, the Pacioli Validating Node software, the Pacioli smart contracts (the \"Smart Contracts\") and the Pacioli Explorer. We refer to this software as a whole as \"Pacioli.\" The Pacioli Validating Node software includes the Pacioli AI Agent (the \"Agent\"), which is described under \"Material aspects of the associated crypto application.\" We refer to any person that uses Pacioli as a \"User.\" Pacioli is infrastructure for the preparation and validation of regulatory disclosures. It serves issuers and servicers of crypto assets that are obligated to prepare disclosures in machine-readable form and to file them with regulatory agencies under emerging regulatory frameworks for crypto assets. Those frameworks include the GENIUS Act and Regulation Crypto Assets (\"Reg CA\") of the Securities and Exchange Commission (the \"Commission\") in the United States, and the Markets in Crypto-Assets Regulation (\"MiCAR\") in the European Union. The Pacioli Explorer is built to give anyone one place to see the validated disclosures of issuers under Reg CA, the GENIUS Act and MiCAR, with a color-coded indicator of compliance for each, the PVNs and MCVs that stand behind it and its on-chain proof. Our aim is for it to become the global destination for disclosure and analysis.</p><p>Auditchain began developing Pacioli in 2021 and launched a minimally viable onchain version in November 2024. Pacioli is currently commercially available as a cloud-based software-as-a-service application. We have offered that service since April 5, 2027, when the Auditchain License became effective. Before that date, Auditchain offered it. Auditchain has also used Pacioli to create proposed machine-readable reporting taxonomies and frameworks, such as the framework used to prepare this document, in response to public requests for comment by regulators.</p><p><strong>The Network.</strong> In its decentralized form, Pacioli runs on a network of nodes (the \"Network\"). Two kinds of nodes operate on the Network. Pacioli Validating Nodes (each, a \"PVN\" and together, the \"PVNs\") validate machine-readable regulatory disclosures. Master conformance validators (each, an \"MCV\" and together, the \"MCVs\") are standard setters that specify data and taxonomy formats. Each MCV acts through one or more qualified delegates that it names. The MCVs test whether each PVN conforms to the logic, data format and taxonomy specifications that apply to PVNs and to the disclosures that PVNs validate (the \"Technical Specifications\"). We refer to each test of a PVN by the MCVs as a \"Conformance Validation.\" A PVN is admitted to the Network only after it passes a Conformance Validation, and it must undergo a Conformance Validation each year. Each person that operates a PVN (an \"Operator\") pays the MCVs an annual fee for Conformance Validations (the \"Conformance Fee\") and a separate fee for the first Conformance Validation of its PVN. The MCVs set those fees and publish them. We do not set them, and this document does not state their amounts. Two standard setters serve as the initial MCVs. We refer to an issuer of crypto assets, or an advisor acting for an issuer, that prepares disclosures in Pacioli as a \"Preparer.\" A User may put a request for validation to the whole Network (the \"open protocol\") or to a private group of PVNs that it engages in place of the whole Network (a \"cohort\").</p><p><strong>AUDT and the Smart Contracts.</strong> The subject crypto asset is the AUDT token (\"AUDT\"), a new ERC20 token. We refer to the Ethereum, Polygon PoS and Robinhood Chain blockchain networks, on which AUDT is or will be deployed, as the \"Underlying Networks.\" AUDT has a maximum supply of 300,000,000, which the Token Contract enforces, and is minted as it is distributed. AUDT is not listed on any trading venue. The Smart Contracts include the AUDT token contract (the \"Token Contract\"), the validation contract (the \"Validation Contract\"), the claims contract (the \"Claims Contract\") and a contract (the \"Subsidies Contract\") that pays a portion of the rewards for validation work as subsidies (\"AUDT Subsidies\"). They also include the validator staking contract, the release contract, the engagement contract and the slash contract, which are described under \"Material aspects of the associated crypto network,\" and the multi-signature contract described below. Four further Smart Contracts will be deployed later than the others. They are the network governance contract (the \"Governance Contract\") and three contracts that are defined below. Unless we state otherwise, a reference in this document to the deployment of the Smart Contracts does not include those four contracts. The addresses of the Smart Contracts are stated under \"Material aspects of the associated crypto network\" and are to be published at https://pacioli.ai.</p><p><strong>Our offerings.</strong> We sell units of a covered investment contract, as that term is defined in Rule 100 of Reg CA (a \"CIC\"). We have structured our capital raising under Reg CA as three offerings. The first is an offering of 70 units of the CIC under the startup exemption of Reg CA (the \"Startup Offering\"). The second is a Tier 2 offering of 670 units of the CIC under the fundraising exemption of Reg CA (the \"Tier 2 Node Offering\" and, together with the Startup Offering, the \"Node Offerings\"). In the Node Offerings, each unit of the CIC is a PVN (a \"Unit\"). A Unit consists of 50,000 AUDT, delivered staked, together with a license to the Pacioli Validating Node software and the right to operate it on the Network. We refer to that license and that right together as the \"Node License.\" We refer to the machine-readable disclosure models for Reg CA, the GENIUS Act and MiCAR as the \"Disclosure Models\" and to the disclosure model for Reg CA as the \"Reg CA Disclosure Model.\" The Auditchain License covers the Disclosure Models. A Unit may not be divided, and the AUDT and the Node License in a Unit may not be separated, with two exceptions, which are described under \"Material terms of the covered investment contract.\" An additional Unit that an Operator purchases under the second exception is not a PVN. The third offering, which we intend to make, is a Tier 2 offering of 22,083,333 AUDT, without a PVN or a Node License, under the fundraising exemption of Reg CA (the \"Tier 2 AUDT Offering\"). We have not filed an offering statement for the Tier 2 AUDT Offering.</p><p>This offering circular relates to the Tier 2 Node Offering, which we also refer to as this \"Offering.\" Harrow Street Securities LLC is our placement agent (the \"Placement Agent\"). It acted in the Startup Offering and acts in the Tier 2 Node Offering. The Auditchain License became effective on April 5, 2027, at the first closing of the Startup Offering.</p><p><strong>Other defined terms.</strong> When our promised essential managerial efforts are complete, we intend to file a transition report on Form TR under Reg CA (\"Form TR\"). We refer to the first 30 PVNs admitted to the Network, not counting any PVN that we operate, as the \"Founding PVNs.\" We refer to a regulatory reporting requirement that is carried on the Network, together with its machine-readable disclosure model, its rules and its tests, as a \"reporting scheme.\"</p><p>Until we give up our keys to the Smart Contracts, a multi-signature contract holds them (the \"Key Holder Contract\"). It has five key holders. We are one, and the other four are Operators of Founding PVNs that are not affiliated with us. We refer to the five as the \"Initial Key Holders.\" We refer to the acts by which we give up those keys, immediately before we file Form TR, as the \"Handover.\" The right to change the settings of the Smart Contracts is not one of those keys. We hold it alone. Our right to change the division of each validation fee among its recipients, the amount of the rewards paid through AUDT Subsidies and the allocation of the proceeds from data subscriptions (together, the \"allocation of rewards\") ends when the Governance Contract is deployed. Our right to change the other settings ends at the Handover. We refer to the signal that we give in the Smart Contracts immediately before we file Form TR, and that opens the functions that wait for that filing, as the \"Form TR Signal.\" The Key Holder Contract, the Handover and the Form TR Signal are described under \"Smart contract governance mechanisms.\"</p><p>We refer to a vote of the holders of AUDT on a proposal that is submitted through the Governance Contract as a \"Governance Vote.\" We refer to the council whose approval every proposal also requires as the \"Governance Council.\" Neither we nor Auditchain, nor any person connected with either of us as described under \"Governance mechanisms,\" may hold a seat on it. The Governance Council records its decisions in a contract (the \"Council Contract\"). The Governance Contract names one address that can cancel a proposal before it is executed (the \"Guardian\"), and that address is the Council Contract. We refer to the registry in which reporting schemes are filed as the \"Scheme Registry,\" and to the contract in which persons that comment on a reporting scheme lock AUDT as the \"Consultation Stake Contract.\" After the filing of Form TR, the Governance Council may also direct the Subsidies Contract to pay rewards to such persons. The Council Contract, the Scheme Registry and the Consultation Stake Contract are the three further Smart Contracts mentioned above. Governance Votes, the Governance Council and the rules for reporting schemes are described under \"Governance mechanisms.\"</p><p>We refer to the security audit by Ironvault Security Labs of the PVN software and of the Smart Contracts, other than the four further Smart Contracts, as the \"Security Audit.\" We refer to the Securities Act of 1933 as the \"Securities Act.\" An \"Accredited Investor\" is an accredited investor as defined in Rule 501 of Regulation D under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.501). An \"LEI\" is a Legal Entity Identifier. A \"vLEI\" is a verifiable LEI credential. Unless we state otherwise, a reference in this document to a \"Rule\" is a reference to a rule of Reg CA as proposed.</p><p><strong>Purpose of this Offering.</strong> We make this Offering primarily to two groups. The first is providers of regulatory disclosure management software and services. The second is issuers of crypto assets that will be required to comply with the technical disclosure specifications under Reg CA and other global standard machine-readable reporting schemes. Each purchaser of a Unit becomes an Operator. We will use the proceeds of this Offering to complete the decentralization of Pacioli and to accelerate its adoption. In this document, the \"decentralization\" of Pacioli means the completion of the six essential managerial efforts that are set out in the table of essential managerial efforts. It has no other meaning. We believe that a decentralized Pacioli will modernize global regulatory disclosure, will meet the demands of the mass migration of the global capital markets onchain, and will make disclosure preparation and validation available 24 hours a day, seven days a week.</p><p><strong>Current status.</strong> The Startup Offering, which began on March 1, 2027, is complete. We sold all 70 Units at five closings, the last on August 27, 2027, and delivered 3,500,000 AUDT staked (see the table of the offering in the previous 12 months on the cover page). On April 5, 2027, we allocated 250,000 AUDT to each of the two initial MCVs. Ironvault Security Labs completed the Security Audit on June 15, 2027. On July 1, 2027, we deployed the Smart Contracts on Ethereum and a bridged Token Contract on Polygon PoS, and the AUDT allocated to the MCVs was minted and staked.</p><p>By August 31, 2027, the Subsidies Contract had paid AUDT Subsidies of 100,000 AUDT to the PVNs on the Network. It can pay no more than 1,000,000 AUDT before the filing of Form TR, and we intend it to pay the remaining 900,000 AUDT over the period until that filing, split equally each month among the active PVNs, as described under \"Plan of development.\" After the $3,500,000 of sales and the $500,000 allocation to the MCVs, those 1,000,000 AUDT take up the rest of the $5,000,000 limit of the startup exemption. We have not awarded any right to claim AUDT from the team or advisor allocations.</p><p>By August 31, 2027, the Founding PVNs had been admitted to the Network after Conformance Validation, and the Network went live on that date. Including our own PVN, 31 PVNs are active. Each of the two MCVs also operates a node. The number of active nodes that we report counts PVNs only. The PVNs of the other 40 Units sold in the Startup Offering have not yet been admitted to the Network.</p><p>Five of the six essential managerial efforts that we promised in our Form 1-SU are complete. The remaining effort, which ends with the Handover, is in progress. Its completion is the trigger for Form TR.</p><p>At the date of this offering circular, 4,150,000 AUDT is outstanding. Persons other than us hold 4,096,774 AUDT: 3,500,000 AUDT sold in the Startup Offering, 500,000 AUDT allocated to the MCVs and 96,774 AUDT paid as AUDT Subsidies. We hold the other 53,226 AUDT: the 50,000 AUDT from the treasury allocation that we have staked for our PVN and 3,226 AUDT of AUDT Subsidies paid to our PVN.</p><p>We activated our Ethereum validator on August 20, 2027. Our application for a Polygon PoS validator and our Robinhood Chain full node will follow.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 52
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT6e5476b30c",
          "@type": "regca:OfferingPeriodDescription",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT6e5476b30c",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 73,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "The offering period is one year from the qualification date (illustratively, October 1, 2027 to September 30, 2028), or until all Units are sold, whichever is earlier. This Offering will commence within two business days after qualification (Rule 300(c)(3)(i)(F)). In addition, this Offering will commence only upon the final adoption of Reg CA by the Commission, or under no-action relief that we may seek from the staff of the Commission in order to conduct this Offering before the final adoption of Reg CA. We would seek that relief in order to prepare the market in advance to comply with Reg CA as finally adopted."
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 53
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT0a2d8066c1",
          "@type": "regca:OfferingPeriodStartDate",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT0a2d8066c1",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 74,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "rdf:value": {
              "@value": "2027-10-01",
              "@type": "xsd:date"
            }
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 54
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT7697c9649f",
          "@type": "regca:OfferingPeriodEndDate",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT7697c9649f",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 75,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "rdf:value": {
              "@value": "2028-09-30",
              "@type": "xsd:date"
            }
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 55
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT92e9c5d7e2",
          "@type": "regca:CoveredInvestmentContractMaterialTerms",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT92e9c5d7e2",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 76,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>This Offering consists of 670 Units at a price of $62,500 per Unit, for an aggregate offering price of $41,875,000. Under Rule 101(e)(2) as proposed, that price is the equivalent of $1.25 per AUDT.</p><p>The CIC in this Offering is sold in Units. Each Unit is a PVN and consists of the following, which are sold together:</p><p>(1) 50,000 AUDT, delivered staked to the purchaser's PVN and locked for a minimum of two years from delivery; and</p><p>(2) a Node License.</p><p>The Node License is the means by which the AUDT invokes the functions of Pacioli. The PVN software is the software that the AUDT stake activates. Except in the cases described below, neither the AUDT stake nor the Node License has a use without the other.</p><p>The Node License is the license to the PVN software, which includes the Agent, and the right to operate that software on the Network. Under the Node License, an Operator may run in production any version of the PVN software that passes Conformance Validation, whoever changed the code, and may validate disclosures under every reporting scheme that the Network carries, without a further license from us or Auditchain and without a further charge by either of us. Neither we nor Auditchain can withdraw those rights while the PVN is staked. The Node License ends when the Operator unstakes. It does not cover LucaSuite™.</p><p>A Unit may not be divided. In this Offering, we do not sell AUDT other than as part of a Unit, or in any amount other than the 50,000 AUDT in a Unit. The AUDT and the Node License in a Unit may not be separated, with two exceptions.</p><p>First, a provider of regulatory disclosure management software or services may purchase a Unit without the Node License if it (i) operates its PVN with its own software, (ii) complies with the Technical Specifications and (iii) submits to the Conformance Validations performed by the MCVs. A Unit purchased under this exception consists of 50,000 AUDT locked in the validator staking contract. The purchaser may validate disclosures under every reporting scheme that the Network carries, without a license from us or Auditchain and without a charge by either of us. The purchase price per Unit does not change, because no part of the purchase price is allocated to the Node License. All other terms of the Unit, and all obligations of the purchaser, are the same, with one addition. A Unit purchased under this exception may be resold only to a provider of regulatory disclosure management software or services that meets the same three conditions. The MCVs confirm that the buyer meets those conditions when they perform the new Conformance Validation.</p><p>Second, an Operator may purchase an additional Unit without the Node License in a Node Offering that is open, for either of two purposes: to restore the stake of its PVN after a penalty, or to stake AUDT for the Preparer discount. An additional Unit consists of 50,000 AUDT, delivered staked and locked for two years, at the price of a Unit. It does not count as a PVN for any purpose: it carries no Conformance Validation, no Conformance Fee and no vote that belongs to a PVN. Its AUDT is applied first to restore the stake of the PVN of the Operator to 50,000 AUDT, and the remainder is staked for the Operator and counts toward the Preparer discount. An additional Unit is one of the Units offered in that Node Offering and does not increase their number. An additional Unit cannot be resold as a Unit. The AUDT that restores the stake becomes part of the stake of the PVN, and the remainder is locked and released on the same terms as AUDT staked for the Preparer discount.</p><p>A purchaser may sell a Unit after two years, subject to two conditions. First, a new Conformance Validation of the PVN must be completed before the sale settles. Second, the buyer must be an Accredited Investor that holds an LEI, if the buyer is an entity, or a vLEI that we have issued, if the buyer is an individual. The parties may agree to the sale while the Conformance Validation is pending, and the sale settles when the Conformance Validation is complete. The two-year lock restarts for the buyer. We do not approve transfers and have no discretion over them. The provider of the identity verification (KYC/AML) service performs the identity and accreditation checks.</p><p>An individual who operates a PVN must hold a vLEI that we issue under our own LEI. We must issue a vLEI to every individual who completes identity verification (KYC/AML). We may refuse or revoke a vLEI only if the individual fails identity verification or ceases to operate a PVN, or if an order of a court or of a regulator, or a rule of the vLEI system, requires it. We will continue to issue vLEIs on these terms after the filing of Form TR.</p><p>Transfers of AUDT from one wallet to another are locked until the day named in the Form TR Signal, as described under \"Other material terms of the covered investment contract.\"</p><p>Rule 100 as proposed defines a CIC as an investment contract to which a crypto asset that is not a security is subject and to which no other asset is subject. A Unit that is sold with the Node License includes that license. In Request for Comment 6, the Commission asks whether the definition should permit an investment contract that involves other assets as well.</p><p>Under Rule 101(e)(1) as proposed, one unit of a CIC would be one AUDT. For that reason, we report the Rule 101(e) measures alongside our Units. Those measures are the number of AUDT per Unit, the equivalent number of AUDT offered and the equivalent price per AUDT. They allow this Offering to be read either way. In its comment letter on proposed Reg CA (Requests for Comment 6, 7 and 31), Auditchain recommends that the definition permit a functional asset such as the Node License, and that an issuer be permitted to define the unit of a CIC as a functional unit of this kind, with any price allocation disclosed. That would allow institutions to establish a network that includes the software that the crypto asset activates.</p><p>No part of the purchase price is allocated to the Node License. The purchase price does not include the initial Conformance Validation of the PVN, which the purchaser pays for separately (see \"Purchaser obligations under the covered investment contract\").</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 56
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT1acec8a34f",
          "@type": "regca:PurchaserObligationsUnderCoveredInvestmentContract",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT1acec8a34f",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 77,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>Each purchaser of a Unit becomes an Operator and has the following obligations.</p><p>(1) Accredited Investor. The purchaser must be an Accredited Investor.</p><p>(2) Identity. The purchaser must complete identity verification (KYC/AML). A purchaser that is an entity must hold an LEI. An individual who operates a PVN must hold a vLEI that we issue, as described under \"Material terms of the covered investment contract.\"</p><p>(3) Conformance Validation. The PVN must pass an initial Conformance Validation before it is admitted to the Network. The PVN must undergo a Conformance Validation each year after that. The annual Conformance Validation covers every reporting scheme that the Network then carries. A PVN is not tested separately for an additional reporting scheme.</p><p>(4) Fees of the MCVs. The Operator must pay the MCVs a fee for the initial Conformance Validation and a Conformance Fee each year. A new Conformance Validation on the sale of a Unit also carries a fee. The MCVs set those fees and publish them. We do not set them, and this document does not state their amounts. None of these fees is included in the purchase price of a Unit.</p><p>(5) Staking. The Operator must keep the 50,000 AUDT delivered with the PVN staked for a minimum of two years from delivery. If the Operator unstakes, the PVN is deactivated immediately and the Node License ends. The former Operator then claims the stake from the release contract in equal daily amounts over two years.</p><p>(6) Slashing. The Operator must accept slashing of the stake in two cases. First, a PVN that does not undergo its annual Conformance Validation forfeits 10 percent of its existing stake. Second, a PVN that withdraws from a validation request after committing to it forfeits 10 percent of its stake on the first withdrawal and 20 percent on the second withdrawal. On each further withdrawal, it forfeits 30 percent and is deactivated for 30 days. The Operator must then restore the stake. The Smart Contracts set no deadline for doing so, and the PVN continues to operate with the reduced stake. The full schedule, the cases in which a PVN is deactivated and the ways in which a stake is restored are described under \"Other material terms of the covered investment contract.\"</p><p>(7) Transfer. The Operator may not transfer the Unit within two years after delivery of the AUDT. A sale after those two years is subject to two conditions. A new Conformance Validation of the PVN must be completed before the sale settles, and the buyer must be an Accredited Investor that holds an LEI or a vLEI. The sale does not require our approval. The two-year lock restarts for the buyer.</p><p>A purchaser that buys a Unit without the Node License under the first exception has the same obligations. In addition, that purchaser may resell the Unit only to a provider of regulatory disclosure management software or services that meets the three conditions of that exception, which is described under \"Material terms of the covered investment contract.\"</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 57
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTd973daf948",
          "@type": "regca:ConditionsToCoveredInvestmentContract",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTd973daf948",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 78,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>The CIC is subject to the following conditions.</p><p>(1) Indivisibility. A Unit may not be divided. In this Offering, we do not sell AUDT other than as part of a Unit, or in any amount other than the 50,000 AUDT in a Unit. The AUDT and the Node License in a Unit may not be separated, except as described under \"Material terms of the covered investment contract.\"</p><p>(2) Delivery of the AUDT. We deployed the Smart Contracts on July 1, 2027, after the Security Audit. For Units sold before that date, we delivered the AUDT staked on that date. For Units sold after that date, we deliver the AUDT staked at the closing of the purchase.</p><p>(3) Delivery of the Node License. We deliver the Node License at the closing of the purchase. The Auditchain License is effective from the first closing of the Startup Offering.</p><p>(4) Admission. A PVN is admitted to the Network only after it passes a Conformance Validation. Until a PVN is admitted, it cannot validate disclosures on the Network. The two-year lock runs from the delivery of the AUDT, whether or not the PVN has been admitted.</p><p>(5) Lock and transfer. The AUDT delivered with a PVN is staked and locked for a minimum of two years from delivery. A purchaser may sell a Unit after two years, subject to two conditions. A new Conformance Validation of the PVN must be completed before the sale settles. The buyer must be an Accredited Investor that holds an LEI, if the buyer is an entity, or a vLEI that we have issued, if the buyer is an individual. The two-year lock then restarts for the buyer. A Unit purchased without the Node License under the first exception may be resold only as described under \"Material terms of the covered investment contract.\"</p><p>(6) Transfers of AUDT. AUDT cannot be transferred from one wallet to another until the day named in the Form TR Signal, as described under \"Other material terms of the covered investment contract.\"</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 58
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTcee58f13db",
          "@type": "regca:OtherMaterialTermsOfCoveredInvestmentContract",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTcee58f13db",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 79,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>Slashing schedule. A PVN that does not undergo its annual Conformance Validation forfeits 10 percent of its existing stake. A PVN is not penalized if its Operator requested the Conformance Validation and paid the Conformance Fee at least 30 days before it was due and the MCVs performed it late. A PVN that undergoes its annual Conformance Validation and does not pass it forfeits nothing. Its Operator has 30 days from the result to cure the deficiencies, and the PVN continues to operate during that time. If the deficiencies are not cured within the 30 days, the MCVs deactivate the PVN. Its stake remains subject to the two-year lock, and the PVN is reactivated when it passes a new Conformance Validation. A PVN that withdraws from a validation request after committing to it forfeits 10 percent of its stake on the first withdrawal, 20 percent on the second withdrawal and 30 percent on each further withdrawal. Each further withdrawal also results in the deactivation of the PVN for 30 days. A separate slash contract administers the forfeitures. It allocates 50 percent of the AUDT forfeited to AUDT Subsidies and 50 percent to the MCVs. It holds the first half and pays it out as AUDT Subsidies only after the Form TR Signal has taken effect.</p><p>Restoring a stake. An Operator whose stake has been reduced by a penalty must restore it. The Operator may do so with AUDT that it has earned on the Network, by purchasing an additional Unit without the Node License in a Node Offering that is open, or by purchasing AUDT in the Tier 2 AUDT Offering while it is open. AUDT that an Operator purchases in the Tier 2 AUDT Offering for that purpose, or to stake for the Preparer discount, will be delivered into the stake in full, without the release schedule of that offering, and locked for two years. The Smart Contracts set no deadline for restoring a stake, and the PVN continues to operate with the reduced stake. From the end of the Tier 2 AUDT Offering until transfers of AUDT open, no AUDT can be bought. After transfers of AUDT open, AUDT may cost more.</p><p>Release schedule on unstaking. When an Operator unstakes, the Node License ends and the former Operator claims the stake from the release contract in equal daily amounts over two years.</p><p>Preparer discount. Staking by a Preparer is optional. A Preparer that stakes 50,000 AUDT receives a 20 percent discount on preparation costs. Each additional 50,000 AUDT staked adds 10 percent to the discount, up to a maximum discount of 50 percent. The stake of a PVN does not count toward the discount. AUDT staked for the discount is locked for two years and is then released on the same terms as the stake of a PVN.</p><p>Preparation. Preparation costs are the prices that we charge a Preparer for preparing disclosures in LucaSuite™. Every Preparer pays them, whether or not it operates a PVN. We set those prices and publish them.</p><p>Transfers of AUDT. Transfers of AUDT are locked until the day named in the Form TR Signal. Until that day, AUDT can move only to and from the Smart Contracts: on delivery, on staking and unstaking, in payment for a validation, as a reward, as a penalty and on a daily release. It cannot be transferred from one wallet to another. A sale of a Unit after two years is not affected, because the stake moves within the validator staking contract. One movement between persons is possible while the lock applies: a User that engages a cohort of PVNs pays the Operators that it has chosen. When we give the Form TR Signal, we name the day on which we intend AUDT to be listed for trading, and the lock ends on that day. That day cannot be earlier than the day on which the Form TR Signal takes effect or more than 14 days after it. It cannot be changed once the Form TR Signal has taken effect, and the lock ends on it whether or not any venue has listed AUDT.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 59
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTc60c7258ef",
          "@type": "regca:FunctionalAssetIncludedIndicator",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTc60c7258ef",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 80,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "rdf:value": {
              "@value": "true",
              "@type": "xsd:boolean"
            }
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 60
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT2ff844b47d",
          "@type": "regca:FunctionalAssetDescription",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT2ff844b47d",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 81,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>The functional asset is the Node License, which is the license to the PVN software and the right to operate it on the Network. We license the preparation and validation software of Pacioli and the Disclosure Models from Auditchain under the Auditchain License. We provide the Node License without charge with the 50,000 AUDT in each Unit. The Node License covers the PVN software that the AUDT stake activates, in every version that passes Conformance Validation, and the validation of disclosures under every reporting scheme that the Network carries. It does not cover LucaSuite™, and it ends when the Operator unstakes. The Unit is the functional unit of the CIC.</p><p>A Unit does not include a Node License if it is purchased under either of the exceptions described under \"Material terms of the covered investment contract.\" A Unit does not include the initial Conformance Validation of the PVN.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 61
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT1f96af71bb",
          "@type": "regca:FunctionalAssetTransferableSeparatelyIndicator",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT1f96af71bb",
