          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 70
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTfe7e77e6af",
          "@type": "regca:PurchasePricePerUnitDeterminationMethod",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTfe7e77e6af",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 91,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "We offer each Unit at $62,500, payable in USDC or USDT. We offer a maximum of 670 Units. Under Rule 101(e)(1) as proposed, one unit of a CIC would be one AUDT. On that basis, the equivalent price per AUDT is $62,500 divided by 50,000, or $1.25. We set the price per Unit. AUDT has no market price. The prices in our offerings are our own choice. They are not based on a market price and are not a measure of the value of AUDT."
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 71
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT14f18e9c5b",
          "@type": "regca:PurchasersLimitedToAccreditedInvestorsIndicator",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT14f18e9c5b",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 92,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "rdf:value": {
              "@value": "true",
              "@type": "xsd:boolean"
            }
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 72
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTb8b24d2dc9",
          "@type": "regca:PurchaserQualificationsOrRestrictions",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTb8b24d2dc9",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 93,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>We make this Offering under the fundraising exemption of Reg CA, 17 CFR 228.300 through 228.307 (Subpart C), as a Tier 2 offering under 17 CFR 228.300(a)(2).</p><p>We make this Offering primarily to two groups. The first is providers of regulatory disclosure management software and services. The second is issuers of crypto assets that will be required to comply with the technical disclosure specifications under Reg CA and other global standard machine-readable reporting schemes.</p><p>We offer Units to purchasers in the United States under Reg CA. We also offer Units to purchasers outside the United States in jurisdictions that are not subject to any United States sanctions.</p><p>Each purchaser must complete identity verification (KYC/AML). A purchaser that is an entity must hold an <strong>LEI</strong>. An individual who operates a PVN must hold a <strong>vLEI</strong> that we issue. We accept payment in USDC or USDT.</p><p><strong>Every purchaser of a Unit must be an Accredited Investor.</strong> Because every purchaser is an Accredited Investor, the 10 percent investment limit of Rule 300(c)(2)(i)(C) does not apply in this Offering. The legend that the form requires appears on the cover.</p><p>This Offering will commence only upon the final adoption of Reg CA by the Commission, or under no-action relief that we may seek from the staff of the Commission in order to conduct this Offering before the final adoption of Reg CA. We would seek that relief in order to prepare the market in advance to comply with Reg CA as finally adopted.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 73
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT98c74e7650",
          "@type": "regca:MaterialDistributionAgreements",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT98c74e7650",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 94,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "We are offering the Units on a \"best efforts\" basis, directly and through the Placement Agent. Neither we nor the Placement Agent is required to sell any minimum number of Units, and the Placement Agent is not required to purchase any Units. Harrow Street Securities LLC, a FINRA member broker-dealer, is the Placement Agent for this Offering under a placement agreement dated August 20, 2027, which is filed as an exhibit to the offering statement. We pay the Placement Agent compensation of 7 percent of gross proceeds, or $2,931,250 if all Units are sold. The compensation is payable at each closing out of the proceeds of that closing. No other agreement in furtherance of the distribution of the Units has been entered into."
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 74
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTf998c07981",
          "@type": "regca:EstimatedOfferingExpenses",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTf998c07981",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 95,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:MonetaryFactValue",
            "cmns-qtu:hasNumericValue": {
              "@value": "3181250",
              "@type": "xsd:decimal"
            },
            "cmns-qtu:hasMeasurementUnit": "iso4217:USD",
            "xbrlb:decimals": "INF"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 75
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT113e8cadd1",
          "@type": "regca:EstimatedNetOfferingProceeds",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT113e8cadd1",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 96,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:MonetaryFactValue",
            "cmns-qtu:hasNumericValue": {
              "@value": "38693750",
              "@type": "xsd:decimal"
            },
            "cmns-qtu:hasMeasurementUnit": "iso4217:USD",
            "xbrlb:decimals": "INF"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 76
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT374f33686a",
          "@type": "regca:IntendedUseOfProceeds",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT374f33686a",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 97,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>We estimate that the net proceeds of this Offering will be $38,693,750 if all Units are sold. That amount is gross proceeds of $41,875,000, less Placement Agent compensation of $2,931,250 and other offering expenses of $250,000.</p><p>We intend to use the net proceeds as follows:</p><p>(1) Marketing: 30% ($11,608,125);</p><p>(2) Development: 20% ($7,738,750);</p><p>(3) Buybacks of AUDT: 10% ($3,869,375);</p><p>(4) Legal and policy: 10% ($3,869,375);</p><p>(5) General and administrative: 20% ($7,738,750); and</p><p>(6) Treasury: 10% ($3,869,375).</p><p>\"Buybacks of AUDT\" means our purchases of AUDT in the secondary market, if and when one develops. We are not obliged to buy any AUDT. AUDT that we buy is not destroyed. We hold it, and it adds to the AUDT that we can vote. \"Treasury\" is cash that we hold in reserve. It includes the cash that we use to buy ETH and POL for staking in our own validators on the Ethereum and Polygon PoS networks (see the section on issuer blockchain network participation). We bought 32 ETH for our Ethereum validator on August 15, 2027. We have not bought any POL. We may use the rest of that reserve for our operations after the filing of Form TR.</p><p>We will begin to use the proceeds upon receipt, except for the amount that we hold in reserve as Treasury. There is no minimum offering amount.</p><p>If we have not spent all of the proceeds by the time we file Form TR, we will continue to use them to fund marketing. After the filing of Form TR, we will also use them to develop data-analytics tools built on Pacioli, which we intend to offer on the same basis as any other third-party developer.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 77
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTd89c6a7fd9",
          "@type": "regca:WhitepaperAndOfferingMaterialsWebsiteAddress",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTd89c6a7fd9",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 110,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "rdf:value": {
              "@value": "https://pacioli.ai",
              "@type": "xsd:anyURI"
            }
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 78
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT6ebca79d73",
          "@type": "regca:SubjectCryptoAssetMaterialAspects",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT6ebca79d73",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 111,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>AUDT is the base utility token of Pacioli. It is a new ERC20 token that is or will be deployed on the Underlying Networks. AUDT has a maximum supply of 300,000,000, which the Token Contract enforces, and is minted as it is distributed. Its ISO 24165 Digital Token Identifier is 7XK9P2D4Q.</p><p>AUDT invokes the functions of the Smart Contracts and of the PVN software in four ways.</p><p>(1) Settlement. A User that requests validation of a disclosure pays the PVNs in AUDT, through the Smart Contracts, and/or in other digital assets that the PVNs accept as payment. There can be no assurance that AUDT will be accepted by PVNs, as described under \"Risk factors.\"</p><p>(2) Staking by Operators. A stake of 50,000 AUDT activates each PVN. The AUDT is delivered staked with the PVN and is locked for a minimum of two years. If the Operator unstakes, the PVN is deactivated at once, the Node License ends and the stake is released in equal daily amounts over two years.</p><p>(3) Staking by Preparers. Staking by a Preparer is optional. A Preparer that stakes 50,000 AUDT receives a 20 percent discount on preparation costs. Each additional 50,000 AUDT staked adds 10 percent to the discount, up to a maximum discount of 50 percent. The stake of a PVN does not count toward the discount. AUDT staked for the discount is locked for two years and is then released on the same terms as the stake of a PVN.</p><p>(4) Governance. Once Governance Votes open, each delegated AUDT carries one vote in a Governance Vote, as described under \"Governance mechanisms.\" AUDT carries a vote when a person holds it in a wallet, or has staked it for a PVN, as an MCV or as a Preparer, and has delegated it. AUDT that the release contract holds, or that is committed to a liquidity pool, carries no vote.</p><p>Stakes are subject to slashing as described under \"Other material terms of the covered investment contract.\" We set the staking requirements until the Handover. Once Governance Votes open, they can be changed only by a Governance Vote together with the approval of the Governance Council.</p><p>AUDT is not listed on any trading venue. Transfers of AUDT from one wallet to another are locked until the day named in the Form TR Signal. We intend to seek trading of AUDT on the venues named in the table of trading venues after the filing of Form TR.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 79
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT6dd18b49dd",
          "@type": "regca:ManagementAndRelatedPersons",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT6dd18b49dd",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 121,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>Jason Meyers is our Chief Executive Officer, our Chief Financial Officer and a director. He is our principal executive officer and our principal financial officer. Thomas Egan, CPA, is our Principal Accounting Officer and a director. Avery Lindqvist is an independent director and was appointed at formation. Our board of directors has three members.</p><p>Mr. Meyers is also Lead Architect of Auditchain, the licensor of Pacioli. He controls both Auditchain and us.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 80
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT6a9621d1d3",
          "@type": "regca:UnitsHeldByRelatedPersons",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT6a9621d1d3",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 157,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-rst:NumericFactValue",
            "cmns-qtu:hasNumericValue": {
              "@value": "0",
              "@type": "xsd:decimal"
            },
            "cmns-qtu:hasMeasurementUnit": "xbrli:pure",
            "xbrlb:decimals": "INF"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 81
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT7fc5806710",
          "@type": "regca:RelatedPersonsSubjectToTransferOrResaleRestrictionsIndicator",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT7fc5806710",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 158,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "rdf:value": {
              "@value": "true",
              "@type": "xsd:boolean"
            }
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 82
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTab45dee025",
          "@type": "regca:RelatedPersonTransferOrResaleRestrictionsDescription",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTab45dee025",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 159,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>A related person that is awarded rights to claim AUDT from the team or advisor allocations can claim AUDT only after the filing of Form TR and only through the Claims Contract. The Claims Contract releases the AUDT of each award in equal daily amounts over two years. The two years begin on the day on which we give the Form TR Signal, which is the day on which we file Form TR, or, for an award made after that day, on the day of the award. The release continues if the related person ceases to serve us. Claimed AUDT is subject to no other lockup, except the lock on transfers of all AUDT until the day named in the Form TR Signal. The restriction end date shown for each related person is two years after December 29, 2028, the day on which we give the Form TR Signal in the timeline of this demonstration.</p><p>A related person that purchases a Unit would be subject to the same two-year lock on the stake, release schedule and transfer conditions as every other purchaser of a Unit. No related person has purchased a Unit.</p><p>We will deliver the 28,250,000 AUDT to Auditchain on or after the day named in the Form TR Signal, because the delivery is a transfer from one wallet to another. No lockup applies to that AUDT once it is delivered.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 83
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT5afbeccc88",
          "@type": "regca:ConflictsOfInterestAndRelatedPersonTransactions",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT5afbeccc88",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 160,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p><strong>The Auditchain License.</strong> Auditchain has granted us a global and exclusive license to Pacioli and the Disclosure Models, with the right to sublicense. Mr. Meyers, our Chief Executive Officer and Chief Financial Officer, is Lead Architect of Auditchain and controls both Auditchain and us. The license agreement is dated September 30, 2026, the date of our incorporation. The Auditchain License became effective on April 5, 2027, at the first closing of the Startup Offering. Its effectiveness was subject to no other condition. The Auditchain License is perpetual and covers future versions of Pacioli. The consideration for the Auditchain License has two parts. The first is 28,250,000 AUDT, which is 50 percent of the treasury allocation and is deliverable to Auditchain after the filing of Form TR. The second is a royalty of 20 percent of the revenue that we derive, in whatever form we receive it, excluding the proceeds of our offerings. No cash is payable for the AUDT component. Auditchain is our related person because it is an affiliate under common control with us. Auditchain remains our licensor after the filing of Form TR. Under each Node License, an Operator may run in production any version of the PVN software that passes Conformance Validation, whoever changed the code, and neither we nor Auditchain can withdraw that right.</p><p><strong>The Initial Key Holders.</strong> Mr. Meyers signs for us as one of the five Initial Key Holders. The other four are Operators of Founding PVNs that are not affiliated with us. Until the Handover, the Key Holder Contract holds our keys to the Smart Contracts, and it cannot act without our signature, as described under \"Smart contract governance mechanisms.\"</p><p><strong>The Governance Council and the Guardian.</strong> Neither we nor Auditchain may hold a seat on the Governance Council, and neither may any of our or its affiliates, founders, directors, officers, employees or advisers. Mr. Meyers holds no seat. The Guardian is the Council Contract. We are never the Guardian.</p><p><strong>Our PVN.</strong> We operate one PVN, staked with 50,000 AUDT from the treasury allocation, and may earn validation rewards as an Operator. Like every other PVN, it receives a share of the AUDT Subsidies; by August 31, 2027, it had received 3,226 AUDT. PVNs that we operate are not counted toward the 30 PVNs of our second promised essential managerial effort. Our PVN has no vote in the election of the Operator members of the Governance Council.</p><p><strong>Minting.</strong> Until the Handover, the Key Holder Contract mints the AUDT delivered in our offerings and the other allocations, up to 136,083,333 AUDT in total, on the signatures described under \"Smart contract governance mechanisms.\" The liquidity allocation is 20,000,000 AUDT and the treasury allocation is 56,500,000 AUDT. Before the Handover, we will mint 12,000,000 AUDT of the liquidity allocation into the three liquidity contracts, which we cannot withdraw from, and the other 8,000,000 AUDT and the treasury allocation in full to ourselves. The right of the Key Holder Contract to mint AUDT ends at the Handover. After it, AUDT can be minted only by the Subsidies Contract, the Claims Contract and the Council Contract, each up to a cap written in its code, as described under \"Supply.\" After we deliver 28,250,000 AUDT to Auditchain, we will retain 36,250,000 AUDT (12.08 percent of the maximum supply), of which 8,000,000 AUDT is for centralized exchanges, and Auditchain will hold 28,250,000 AUDT (9.42 percent). No lockup applies to the AUDT held by either of us, other than the lock on transfers of all AUDT described under \"Lockups\" and the two-year lock on the 50,000 AUDT staked for our PVN.</p><p><strong>Settings and fees.</strong> Until the Governance Contract is deployed, we alone set the allocation of rewards, which includes the rate of AUDT Subsidies and the division of each validation fee among its recipients. Until the Handover, we alone set the other settings of the Smart Contracts, including the stake of a PVN. We can change each of them at any time until then, and a change can raise or lower what an Operator earns.</p><p><strong>Voting power.</strong> No more than 137,083,333 AUDT will be outstanding when we file Form TR. We will then hold at least 47.1 percent of the AUDT outstanding. That share counts the 8,000,000 AUDT for centralized exchanges and does not count the 12,000,000 AUDT in the liquidity contracts, which we do not control and which carries no vote. Governance Votes open when the Form TR Signal takes effect. From then, we and Auditchain may delegate and vote the AUDT that we hold like any other holder. As for every holder, AUDT that either of us holds on a centralized exchange must first be withdrawn to a wallet that we control and delegated. If we delegate and vote our 64,500,000 AUDT, we can defeat any proposal put to a Governance Vote and carry any settings proposal, and we can carry any general proposal unless more than 32,250,000 votes are cast against it. While the 8,000,000 AUDT is on centralized exchanges, we can cast 56,500,000 votes, and other holders could carry or defeat a settings proposal if they cast more votes than we do. We cannot block a mint from the reserve, which needs no Governance Vote. We cannot carry out any proposal without the approval of the Governance Council. After we deliver 28,250,000 AUDT to Auditchain, the same is true of us and Auditchain together. The risk factors describe this further.</p><p><strong>Payments and royalties.</strong> We are not a party to direct payments between Users and Operators. We receive no part of those payments, except that the PVN that we operate may earn a share of them on the same terms as every other PVN. We pay Auditchain the royalty of 20 percent of our revenue described above, which excludes the proceeds of our offerings. The royalty accrues on our staking rewards, on any validation rewards that our PVN earns, including rewards paid in AUDT, and on the preparation costs that Preparers pay us. The royalty on AUDT Subsidies and other rewards paid to our PVN in AUDT is paid in AUDT, after the day named in the Form TR Signal. The royalty also accrues on the trading fees that the liquidity contracts pay us.</p><p><strong>Auditchain's activities.</strong> Auditchain receives no taxonomy-developer rewards for the Disclosure Models that it developed. Auditchain operates its own validator on Ethereum and intends to operate its own validator on Polygon PoS and its own full node on Robinhood Chain, as we do. It earns staking rewards on the same basis as any other participant in those networks (see the sections on issuer and affiliate blockchain network participation). Auditchain does not operate a PVN. Auditchain is the developer of the Reg CA Disclosure Model, which is the first reporting scheme. Only the person that filed a reporting scheme, or the regulator or standard setter whose requirement it carries, can file a change to it. Neither we nor Auditchain, nor any person that is excluded from the Governance Council because of its connection with either of us, may act as the delegate of an MCV.</p><p><strong>The MCVs.</strong> The MCVs receive one half of every penalty that is taken from the stake of a PVN. That includes the penalty for a PVN that does not undergo its annual Conformance Validation, which the MCVs or their delegates perform, so that an MCV could gain from its own delay. For that reason, a PVN is not penalized if its Operator requested the Conformance Validation and paid the Conformance Fee at least 30 days before it was due and the MCVs performed it late. The MCVs will also hold seats on the Governance Council. Each of the two initial MCVs received its stake of 250,000 AUDT from us without cost, for establishing the Network. After the filing of Form TR, we may give a later MCV its stake out of our treasury allocation.</p><p><strong>Our activities after the filing of Form TR.</strong> After the Handover, we will keep two rights in the Smart Contracts: the right to name the recipients of the team and advisor allocations, and the Form TR Signal. Outside the Smart Contracts, we will continue to hold the Auditchain License, to charge preparation costs and to issue vLEIs, and Auditchain will remain our licensor. After the filing of Form TR, we may develop taxonomies and data-analytics tools and participate in the Network on the same basis as any other third party, with four exceptions. We may not hold a seat on the Governance Council. Our PVN has no vote in the election of its Operator members. We cannot be paid consultation rewards. We may not act as the delegate of an MCV. As a developer of taxonomies, we may then earn royalties on the same basis as any other developer.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 84
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT7de1e0c723",
          "@type": "regca:AssociatedCryptoNetworkMaterialAspects",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT7de1e0c723",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 161,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>AUDT and the Smart Contracts are based on Ethereum and are developed in Solidity.</p><p>The Token Contract is deployed on Ethereum at 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d70001. It was deployed on July 1, 2027. A bridged deployment at the same address exists on Polygon PoS, where it was deployed on July 1, 2027. A bridged deployment at the same address on Robinhood Chain is planned before the Handover. Robinhood Chain is an Ethereum layer-2 network built on the Arbitrum Orbit (Nitro) stack.</p><p>The other Smart Contracts that we deployed on July 1, 2027 are on Ethereum at the following addresses: the Subsidies Contract at 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d70002; the Validation Contract at 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d70003; the Claims Contract at 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d70004; the validator staking contract, which holds the stakes of PVNs, MCVs and Preparers, at 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d70009; the release contract, which releases AUDT in daily amounts, at 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7000a; the engagement contract, through which a User requests a validation, at 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7000b; the slash contract, which administers penalties, at 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7000c; and the Key Holder Contract at 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7000d. The Security Audit covered each of them.</p><p>Each deployment can be verified on a public block explorer by its transaction identifier (TXID). The TXIDs of the deployments on Ethereum on July 1, 2027 are: the Token Contract, 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a00001 (https://etherscan.io/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a00001); the Subsidies Contract, 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a00002 (https://etherscan.io/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a00002); the Validation Contract, 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a00003 (https://etherscan.io/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a00003); the Claims Contract, 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a00004 (https://etherscan.io/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a00004); the validator staking contract, 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a00009 (https://etherscan.io/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a00009); the release contract, 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0000a (https://etherscan.io/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0000a); the engagement contract, 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0000b (https://etherscan.io/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0000b); the slash contract, 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0000c (https://etherscan.io/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0000c); and the Key Holder Contract, 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0000d (https://etherscan.io/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0000d). The TXID of the bridged deployment of the Token Contract on Polygon PoS on July 1, 2027 is 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a01001 (https://polygonscan.com/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a01001). The Key Holder Contract was also deployed on Polygon PoS on July 1, 2027, at the same address; the TXID of that deployment is 0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0100d (https://polygonscan.com/tx/0xd7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0100d).</p><p>The Governance Contract, the Council Contract, the Scheme Registry and the Consultation Stake Contract have not been deployed. Their addresses are determined in advance and are 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d70005, 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d70006, 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d70007 and 0xa0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d7a0d70008. The timelock that carries out proposals is part of the Governance Contract and has the same address. We will deploy those four contracts with the counsel of the Founding PVNs, after a second audit of their code and of every change that they require in the Smart Contracts already deployed.</p><p>Each Smart Contract is subject to the consensus mechanism of the Underlying Network on which it is deployed. Ethereum and Polygon PoS use proof of stake. Robinhood Chain uses a single sequencer, operated by the operator of the chain, with fraud proofs posted to Ethereum.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 85
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT07b31f47c6",
          "@type": "regca:AssociatedCryptoApplicationMaterialAspects",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT07b31f47c6",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 162,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>Pacioli is designed as a decentralized protocol for preparing and validating regulatory disclosures. It has two functions.</p><p>Preparation. Preparers prepare machine-readable disclosures in Pacioli from disclosure models published by standard setters and regulators.</p><p>Validation. Independent PVNs check each disclosure against the Technical Specifications that apply to the reporting scheme under which it was prepared. Those specifications are the XBRL 2.1 and XBRL Formula specifications, the Open Information Model and xBRL-JSON (Project Tavi), the Reg CA Disclosure Model, and all other disclosure models based on the XBRL specifications.</p><p>Two kinds of nodes operate on the Network.</p><p>(1) MCVs. Two standard setters serve as the initial MCVs. Other global standard setters that specify data and taxonomy formats may also serve as MCVs. The two initial MCVs are named in the Smart Contracts at their deployment. No person holds a right to admit or remove an MCV before Governance Votes open. After that, an MCV is admitted or removed only by a Governance Vote together with the approval of the Governance Council. Each MCV must name at least one qualified delegate to perform its Conformance Validations on time, and the MCV decides who is qualified. Neither we nor Auditchain, nor any person that is excluded from the Governance Council because of its connection with either of us, may act as a delegate. The MCVs verify that each PVN conforms to the Technical Specifications. A PVN is admitted to the Network only after it passes a Conformance Validation, and it must undergo a Conformance Validation each year. Each MCV operates a node and stakes 250,000 AUDT. We allocated 250,000 AUDT to each of the two initial MCVs outside our offerings, without cost, for establishing the Network. That allocation counts toward the $5,000,000 limit of the startup exemption. After the filing of Form TR, we may give a later MCV its stake out of our treasury allocation. We have not promised to do so. The MCVs earn the fees that Operators pay for Conformance Validations, a share of each validation fee and one half of the penalties taken from the stakes of PVNs. The MCVs pay no fees.</p><p>(2) PVNs. PVNs validate and analyze the regulatory disclosures that issuers of crypto assets prepare under Reg CA and under other reporting schemes. The Agent is part of the PVN software on every PVN. It uses an algorithm that is designed to search for, detect and fulfill requests for the validation or analysis of machine-readable crypto asset white papers and financial statements. Each PVN continuously scans the Network for such requests. When a request is detected, the Agent initiates a race among the PVNs to fulfill it. The Agent also governs how the other PVNs reach consensus with the PVN that wins the race. The Agent allocates the rewards to the winning PVN and to the other PVNs that reach consensus with, and corroborate, the winning PVN. The share of a validation fee for the corroborating PVNs is divided equally among them.</p><p>The software that we license with each PVN is the means by which Operators participate in Pacioli. An Operator that purchases a Unit without the Node License under the first exception participates through its own software, which must comply with the Technical Specifications and must perform the functions of the Agent.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 86
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT7845ec046d",
          "@type": "regca:PlanOfDevelopment",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT7845ec046d",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 163,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>We deployed the Subsidies Contract on July 1, 2027, with the Token Contract, the Validation Contract and the Claims Contract. The Subsidies Contract pays AUDT Subsidies in order to accelerate the adoption of Pacioli.</p><p>We will report the final transition on Form TR upon the occurrence of three events: the final deployment of the Subsidies Contract, the adoption of a minimum of 30 PVNs, and the deployment of the Governance Contract with the counsel of the Founding PVNs, together with the other steps of our sixth promised effort, which ends with the Handover. The first two of those events have occurred. A sample model of Form TR is provided to the staff of the Commission for demonstration purposes.</p><p>The Startup Offering also funded three other efforts. The first is the onboarding of two standard setters as the initial MCVs. The second is the deployment of the Reg CA Disclosure Model to Pacioli as the first reporting scheme. The third is the Security Audit, which we obtained before we deployed the Smart Contracts and the PVN software.</p><p>The Subsidies Contract caps the AUDT Subsidies paid before the filing of Form TR at 1,000,000 AUDT, or $1,000,000 at the equivalent price of $1.00 per AUDT in the Startup Offering. That amount is the capacity remaining under the $5,000,000 limit of the startup exemption after the Startup Offering and the allocation to the MCVs. We set the rate at which the Subsidies Contract pays AUDT Subsidies, and we can raise or lower it until the Governance Contract is deployed. We have set the rate so that the Subsidies Contract pays the 1,000,000 AUDT over the whole period from the deployment of the Smart Contracts on July 1, 2027 until the filing of Form TR. Each month, the Subsidies Contract splits the AUDT Subsidies for that month equally among the active PVNs. A PVN is active in a month if, in that month, it validates or analyzes disclosures as the winning PVN or as a corroborating PVN. A PVN that is not active in a month receives no AUDT Subsidies for that month. The more PVNs are active, the smaller the share of each. By August 31, 2027, the Subsidies Contract had paid 100,000 AUDT of AUDT Subsidies. From the deployment of the Governance Contract, the rate of AUDT Subsidies is subject to governance. No person can change it until Governance Votes open. After that, a change to the rate is a settings proposal: it must be put to a Governance Vote of the holders of AUDT and must also receive the approval of the Governance Council. Our PVN receives AUDT Subsidies on the same terms as every other PVN.</p><p>After the filing of Form TR, the Governance Council may also direct the Subsidies Contract to pay consultation rewards to persons that comment on a reporting scheme, as described under \"Governance mechanisms.\" Consultation rewards cannot exceed 4,500,000 AUDT in total, and the Governance Council is not obliged to pay any.</p><p>We may award rights to claim AUDT from the team and advisor allocations at any time, because the Token Contract, the Subsidies Contract and the Claims Contract are deployed. No AUDT can be claimed under such a right until after the filing of Form TR.</p><p>We and our affiliate Auditchain each operate one validator on Ethereum and intend to operate one validator on Polygon PoS and a full node on Robinhood Chain (see the sections on issuer and affiliate blockchain network participation). The purpose is for the Underlying Networks to be secured in part by the participants in Pacioli.</p><p>Liquidity. Of the net proceeds of the Tier 2 AUDT Offering, we will use $30,000,000 of USDC, with the 20,000,000 AUDT of the liquidity allocation, to provide liquidity at $1.50 per AUDT when transfers of AUDT open. Before the Handover, we will deploy three liquidity contracts, one on each Underlying Network, mint 12,000,000 AUDT into them (6,000,000 AUDT on Ethereum and, through the bridge, 4,000,000 AUDT on Robinhood Chain and 2,000,000 AUDT on Polygon PoS) and send them $18,000,000 of USDC in the same proportions. On the day on which transfers of AUDT open, any person may call each liquidity contract to deposit its AUDT and USDC in a Uniswap AUDT/USDC pool on its network. The contract then holds the pool position permanently: no one, including us, can withdraw it. It pays us the trading fees that the position earns, which are revenue on which we pay Auditchain its royalty. We will place the other 8,000,000 AUDT and $12,000,000 of USDC with Coinbase (3,000,000 AUDT and $4,500,000), Kraken (2,500,000 AUDT and $3,750,000) and OKX (2,500,000 AUDT and $3,750,000) if they list AUDT. We will provide no liquidity on Robinhood, which is a broker trading application; its customers can reach the pool on Robinhood Chain. This is our intention, not a promise of essential managerial efforts.</p><p>This Offering is expansion capital to accelerate the adoption of Pacioli. It adds no promise of essential managerial efforts to the six that are set out in the table of essential managerial efforts. The Network operates with the Founding PVNs under Conformance Validation. At this stage, however, the Network still depends on the cooperation of the MCVs and the Founding PVNs. Our managerial efforts therefore continue through this Offering.</p><p>We will use the net proceeds as described under \"Intended use of proceeds\" to accelerate adoption toward a Network of 740 PVNs. We believe that a Network of that size is sufficient to handle the filing obligations of the world's issuers across the reporting schemes that the Network validates.</p><p>Our one remaining promised effort is the sixth effort in the table of essential managerial efforts: to deploy the Governance Contract, the Council Contract, the Scheme Registry and the Consultation Stake Contract with the counsel of the Founding PVNs and after a second audit, to seat the first Governance Council and to carry out the Handover. After the Handover, the code and the settings of the Smart Contracts can be changed only by a Governance Vote together with the approval of the Governance Council. We intend to file Form TR immediately after the Handover.</p><p>The Key Holder Contract mints the AUDT that we deliver in our offerings, and its right to mint ends at the Handover. We therefore intend to carry out the Handover only after this Offering and the Tier 2 AUDT Offering have ended. Our target date for the Handover and for the filing of Form TR is December 31, 2028. It is a target, and we do not promise it.</p><p>As the issuer of the Units described under \"Material terms of the covered investment contract\" (regca:CoveredInvestmentContractMaterialTerms), we have structured this Offering in a form that issuers and users of crypto assets already know. That form is a validator node that is activated by a stake of the network's token, earns rewards for work that the network can verify and is slashed for work that it fails to do. The Units carry the same kinds of incentives as the production versions of other decentralized protocols, applied to regulatory disclosure. Those incentives are staking, validation rewards, royalties, slashing and governance.</p><p>We believe that compliance with Reg CA will be adopted faster if the disclosures that it requires are prepared and validated through a protocol whose economics are familiar to the people who must comply. This Offering is intended to accelerate the adoption of the Reg CA exemptions and of Pacioli.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 87
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTf30cc667a9",
          "@type": "regca:NumberOfActiveNodesOnNetworkOrApplication",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTf30cc667a9",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 164,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-rst:NumericFactValue",
            "cmns-qtu:hasNumericValue": {
              "@value": "31",
              "@type": "xsd:decimal"
            },
            "cmns-qtu:hasMeasurementUnit": "xbrli:pure",
            "xbrlb:decimals": "INF"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 88
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTf62e03a311",
          "@type": "regca:SecurityMaterialAspects",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTf62e03a311",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 191,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>We license Pacioli from Auditchain. The Smart Contracts are open source. The PVN software, which includes the Agent, is not open source. Its source code is public under the Business Source License 1.1. That license permits a person to copy and modify the code and to use it other than in production. It does not by itself permit production use, and each version becomes available under an open-source license no later than the fourth anniversary of its first public distribution. The Node License permits each Operator to run the PVN software in production. The source code of LucaSuite™ and of the Pacioli Explorer is not public. The source code of the Smart Contracts and of the PVN software is public at https://github.com/Auditchain/. The terms of the Business Source License 1.1 that apply to each version of the PVN software are stated with the published code.</p><p>Ironvault Security Labs completed the Security Audit on June 15, 2027, before the Smart Contracts were deployed on July 1, 2027. The Security Audit found no critical or high-severity issues. The report on the Security Audit is published at https://pacioli.ai/security.</p><p>A second audit will cover the Governance Contract, the Council Contract, the Scheme Registry, the Consultation Stake Contract and every change that they require in the Smart Contracts already audited. We will obtain it before we deploy those four contracts.</p><p>No SOC or ISAE attestation covers the Network. Vendors that build on the Network are responsible for their own attestations. Whether a decentralized network can obtain such an attestation will remain unsettled until the audit standards become clear.</p><p>The MCVs test the conformance of each PVN to the Technical Specifications before the PVN is admitted to the Network and each year after that.</p>"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 89
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTb2c13fc266",
