        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTb9d55958e8-5",
          "@type": "regca:EssentialManagerialEffortProgressDescription",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTb9d55958e8-5",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 843,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasTime": "regca-1crypto:period/2027-09-01",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "In progress. The Founding PVNs have been admitted. We will deploy the Governance Contract, the Council Contract, the Scheme Registry and the Consultation Stake Contract with the counsel of the Founding PVNs and after the second audit, seat the first Governance Council and carry out the Handover."
          },
          "regca:EssentialManagerialEffortIdentifierTypedAxis": 6,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 807
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT75d67b9a35-0",
          "@type": "regca:FinancialStatementNoteNumber",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT75d67b9a35-0",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 925,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasDatePeriod": "regca-1crypto:period/2026-09-30--2026-12-31",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "1",
            "xbrlb:jsonValueKind": "number"
          },
          "regca:FinancialStatementNoteIdentifierTypedAxis": 1,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 808
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT378b2deaae-0",
          "@type": "regca:FinancialStatementNoteTitle",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT378b2deaae-0",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 926,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasDatePeriod": "regca-1crypto:period/2026-09-30--2026-12-31",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "Organization"
          },
          "regca:FinancialStatementNoteIdentifierTypedAxis": 1,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 809
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT2758c66517-0",
          "@type": "regca:FinancialStatementNoteText",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT2758c66517-0",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 927,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasDatePeriod": "regca-1crypto:period/2026-09-30--2026-12-31",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>Pacioli Labs, Inc. (the \"Company\") was formed in Delaware on September 30, 2026. Capitalized terms that are used in these notes and are not defined in them have the meanings given to them under \"Current stage of development\" in this document.</p><p>The Company holds the Auditchain License from Auditchain, an affiliate under common control with the Company (Note 5). Jason Meyers controls both companies. The Auditchain License is perpetual, global and exclusive. It covers Pacioli and the Disclosure Models, includes future versions and gives the Company the right to sublicense.</p><p>The Company sells Units of a CIC under Reg CA. Each Unit is a PVN and consists of 50,000 AUDT, delivered staked, with a Node License. A provider of regulatory disclosure management software or services may purchase a Unit without the Node License on the conditions that this document describes.</p><p>Pacioli is designed as a decentralized protocol for the preparation and validation of machine-readable regulatory disclosures. The Network went live on August 31, 2027 with the Founding PVNs. The Company also operates one PVN and one validator on the Ethereum network.</p>"
          },
          "regca:FinancialStatementNoteIdentifierTypedAxis": 1,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 810
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTbb707ea10a-1",
          "@type": "regca:FinancialStatementNoteNumber",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTbb707ea10a-1",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 928,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasDatePeriod": "regca-1crypto:period/2026-09-30--2026-12-31",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "2",
            "xbrlb:jsonValueKind": "number"
          },
          "regca:FinancialStatementNoteIdentifierTypedAxis": 2,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 811
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT14a75d815f-1",
          "@type": "regca:FinancialStatementNoteTitle",
          "dct:identifier": "FACT14a75d815f-1",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 929,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasDatePeriod": "regca-1crypto:period/2026-09-30--2026-12-31",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "Basis of presentation and significant accounting policies"
          },
          "regca:FinancialStatementNoteIdentifierTypedAxis": 2,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 812
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACTc42c599641-1",
          "@type": "regca:FinancialStatementNoteText",
          "dct:identifier": "FACTc42c599641-1",
          "sbrm-mm:sequence": 930,
          "sbrm-rev:isReportedBy": "regca-1crypto:party/5067001J8OL3RK15TE82/role",
          "cmns-dt:hasDatePeriod": "regca-1crypto:period/2026-09-30--2026-12-31",
          "sbrm-rst:hasFactValue": {
            "@type": "sbrm-frst:NonNumericFactValue",
            "cmns-txt:hasTextValue": "<p>The financial statements are prepared in accordance with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States (U.S. GAAP). The Company's fiscal year ends on December 31. The first fiscal period ran from formation on September 30, 2026 to December 31, 2026.</p><p><strong>Use of estimates.</strong> The preparation of financial statements requires estimates that affect the reported amounts. The significant estimates are the fair value of AUDT issued for services, the fair value of the crypto assets that the Company holds, and the income tax rate.</p><p><strong>Characterization of the Units for accounting purposes.</strong> Reg CA treats the Units that the Company sells as securities (CICs) for the purposes of the Securities Act. That characterization governs the Company's disclosure obligations. It does not determine the accounting. The Units are not equity of the Company, because holders have no residual interest in the Company. The Units are not financial liabilities, because the Company has no obligation to deliver cash or other financial assets to holders. The Units are contracts with customers for the delivery of goods and services within the scope of ASC 606. Those goods and services are AUDT, the Node License and participation in an operating Network. The two characterizations do not conflict. The aggregate offering price reported under Reg CA equals the revenue recognized when the Units are delivered. The offering expenses reported under Reg CA are the Placement Agent compensation, which is shown as cost of revenue, and the other offering expenses, which are shown in operating expenses.</p><p><strong>Revenue recognition (ASC 606).</strong> The Company's revenue recognition policies cover three sources: (a) Units, (b) AUDT sold alone and (c) staking rewards.</p><p>(a) Units. The Company applies the five steps of ASC 606 as follows.</p><p>Step 1, contract. Each Unit purchase and license agreement, approved by both parties, is a contract with a customer. The promises in the Company's disclosures on Form 1-SU and Form 1-CRYPTO are promises implied by the Company's published statements and form part of the contract (ASC 606-10-25-16).</p><p>Step 2, performance obligations. The Company promises (i) 50,000 AUDT delivered staked, (ii) a Node License, unless the Unit is purchased without the Node License (Note 1), and (iii) an operating Network in which the PVN can be admitted and earn rewards. An operating Network means that the Founding PVNs are under Conformance Validation and that the Subsidies Contract and the Reg CA Disclosure Model are deployed. None of these promises is distinct from the others. The staked AUDT cannot be used without PVN software, the PVN software has no use without an operating Network, and the purchaser cannot benefit from any one of them on its own (ASC 606-10-25-19). The nature of the promise is to transfer a combined item (ASC 606-10-25-21). The three promises are therefore combined into a single performance obligation (ASC 606-10-25-22). The deployment of the Governance Contract that is promised in the plan of development is an activity that the Company undertakes for the Network as a whole. It transfers no good or service to a purchaser and is not a performance obligation (ASC 606-10-25-17).</p><p>Step 3, transaction price. The transaction price is the fixed Unit price, which is $50,000 in the Startup Offering and $62,500 in the Tier 2 Node Offering. The Company receives the price in USDC or USDT and converts it to U.S. dollars on receipt (ASC 606-10-32-2). The Company pays the compensation of the Placement Agent out of the proceeds. That compensation does not reduce the transaction price.</p><p>Step 4, allocation. The entire price is allocated to the single performance obligation.</p><p>Step 5, recognition. The performance obligation is satisfied at a point in time (ASC 606-10-25-30). The Node License is a right to use intellectual property, which is satisfied at a point in time (ASC 606-10-55-58B). The point in time is when the purchaser obtains control of a delivered, staked PVN in an operating Network (ASC 606-10-25-23). For Units sold before the Network began operating, that point was August 31, 2027. By that date, the Founding PVNs had been admitted, and on that date the Network went live as the minimally viable Network of the plan of development. For Units sold after that date, that point is delivery at the closing. Consideration received before that point is presented as a contract liability (ASC 606-10-45-2).</p><p>Alternative considered and rejected. The Company considered deferring all Unit revenue until it files Form TR, on the view that its remaining plan-of-development promise is part of what purchasers paid for. The Company rejected that view for two reasons. First, once the Network operates, purchasers direct the use of their PVNs and obtain the benefits of their PVNs without further action by the Company. Those benefits are validation work, rewards and staking. Second, the Governance Contract benefits the Network generally and does not transfer a good or service to a purchaser (ASC 606-10-25-17). Control therefore transfers at the launch of the Network and not upon the filing of Form TR.</p><p>(b) AUDT sold alone. The Company intends to make the Tier 2 AUDT Offering, in which each unit of the CIC will be one AUDT. Of each purchase, 20 percent will be delivered to the purchaser's wallet at closing and 80 percent will be delivered at closing to a release contract. Those units will carry no PVN, Node License or Network promise. The Company will recognize the revenue when the AUDT is delivered to the purchaser or to the release contract, which acts for the purchaser. The Company had sold no AUDT in the Tier 2 AUDT Offering at the dates of these statements.</p><p>(c) Staking rewards. The Company activated its validator on the Ethereum network on August 20, 2027 and receives ETH as rewards for operating it. It will receive POL as rewards for the validator that it intends to operate on the Polygon PoS network. The Company recognizes those rewards as revenue when it receives them, measured at the fair value of the units on that date. That fair value becomes their cost basis. The Company had received no staking rewards at the dates of these statements.</p><p>The Company also charges Preparers for preparing disclosures in LucaSuite™, at prices that it publishes. It had no revenue from preparation in the periods presented.</p><p><strong>Costs to obtain contracts (ASC 340-40).</strong> The Company pays the Placement Agent compensation of 7 percent of gross proceeds at each closing. That compensation is an incremental cost of obtaining a contract (ASC 340-40-25-2). Where the related revenue is deferred, the Company recognizes the compensation as an asset (ASC 340-40-25-1), presents it in other assets and expenses it as cost of revenue when the revenue is recognized (ASC 340-40-35-1). Where the revenue is recognized at the closing, the Company expenses the compensation at the closing. The Company expenses other offering expenses as incurred.</p><p><strong>Crypto assets (ASC 350-60).</strong> The Company measures crypto assets other than AUDT at fair value at each reporting date. It held none at the dates of these statements. It recognizes changes in fair value in net income and presents them separately from changes in the carrying amount of other intangible assets (ASC 350-60-35-1, 350-60-45-1, 350-60-45-2). The Company determines cost basis by specific identification. It measures rewards received at fair value on receipt (ASC 350-60-50-2). AUDT that the Company mints for its own account is a self-created intangible asset. That AUDT is the stake of the Company's PVN, the AUDT Subsidies paid to that PVN and, before the filing of Form TR, the treasury allocation and the 8,000,000 AUDT of the liquidity allocation for centralized exchanges. The Company does not recognize that AUDT. It discloses it.</p><p><strong>AUDT issued for services.</strong> The Company delivers AUDT to the MCVs for establishing the Network and pays AUDT Subsidies to Operators for validation work. The Company recognizes that AUDT as an expense as the services are received. It measures the expense at $1.00 per AUDT, which is the equivalent price per AUDT at which it sold Units in the Startup Offering. AUDT that the Subsidies Contract pays to the Company's own PVN is not recognized as an expense or as an asset, because the Company does not recognize its own AUDT. The royalty that the Company owes Auditchain on those AUDT, 20 percent, is payable in AUDT after transfers of AUDT open. The Company recognizes it as royalty expense at $1.00 per AUDT and as an obligation to deliver the subject crypto asset. The Company uses the same amount to count these issuances toward the $5,000,000 limit of the startup exemption. Where a mixture of cash and non-cash consideration is to be received, Rule 100 of Reg CA bases the aggregate offering price on the price at which the CIC is offered for cash. The Company credits contributed capital, by analogy to equity-classified awards under ASC 718 (ASC 718-10-25-2). That treatment rests on three facts. The AUDT delivered imposes no obligation on the Company to transfer cash or other financial assets. The recipients perform services for the Network. No asset is derecognized, because self-created AUDT is not recognized. The Company considered recognizing a contract liability and rejected that alternative, because the Company has no remaining performance obligation to the recipients once the Network operates. These issuances are noncash transactions. They are excluded from the statement of cash flows and are disclosed in these notes (ASC 230-10-50-4).</p><p><strong>Transactions with entities under common control.</strong> The Company records assets acquired from an entity under common control with the Company at their carrying amounts in the accounts of the transferring entity at the date of transfer, and not at fair value. The Company records the obligation incurred as consideration at the same amount and recognizes no gain or loss. An agreement that is not yet effective is not recognized but is disclosed (Note 5).</p><p><strong>Obligation to deliver AUDT.</strong> An obligation to deliver units of AUDT that the Company has not yet minted is a liability until the units are delivered and the Company is relieved of the obligation (ASC 405-20-40-1). The Company recognized no such liability at the dates of these statements (Note 5).</p><p><strong>Income taxes (ASC 740).</strong> Income tax expense is the current tax on taxable income at an estimated combined federal and state rate of 27 percent. The Company uses that rate as a placeholder until its state apportionment is determined. The 2026 operating loss gave rise to a deferred tax asset. The Company recorded a full valuation allowance against that asset at December 31, 2026, because it was not more likely than not that a startup with no revenue would realize it. The Company expects to use the loss in 2027. No other temporary differences existed at the dates of these statements. The Company therefore recognizes no deferred tax assets or liabilities.</p><p><strong>Related persons (ASC 850).</strong> Transactions with Auditchain, an affiliate under common control with the Company, are described in Note 5.</p>"
          },
          "regca:FinancialStatementNoteIdentifierTypedAxis": 2,
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 813
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:fact/FACT478ce94e17-2",
